  "commit_message": "Show the full two-line output of `black --version` in the docs (#5555)\n\ndocs: show the full two-line output of `black --version`\n\nThe `--version` examples in the_basics.md print a single line, but the\nclick `version_option` message in `src/black/__init__.py` ends with a\nnewline followed by\n`Python ({platform.python_implementation()}) {platform.python_version()}`,\nso the actual output is two lines. The reference-section example also\nomits the `(compiled: ...)` suffix that the same command prints ",
